WEBVTT

00:00:25.670 --> 00:00:28.970
Gobble!! Guts!! Gobble!! Guts!! Gobble!!

00:00:30.810 --> 00:00:34.210
Gobble!! Guts!! Gobble!! Guts!! Gobble!!

00:00:36.410 --> 00:00:39.050
Calling everything delicious!

00:00:39.050 --> 00:00:43.550
The more I eat, the more powerful I get!

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:46.920
Let’s capture ingredients around the world!

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:51.500
I dream of being an invincible 
Gourmet Fighter!!

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:56.530
Now on to the bottom of the 
sea, or the tops of glaciers!

00:00:56.530 --> 00:00:59.200
Jump! Jump Jump Jump! 
Knock! Knock Knock Knock!

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:01.400
Give thanks!

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:04.610
Let’s eat!

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:10.410
Wow wo!! Spiked Punch! Wow wo!! Multi-fold!

00:01:10.410 --> 00:01:15.550
Guts! Gutsy Guts! I can eat any dream!

00:01:15.550 --> 00:01:20.820
Wow wo!! My very own... 
Wow wo!! ...Full Course!

00:01:21.090 --> 00:01:24.990
Guts! Gutsy Guts! Gather them all up!

00:01:24.990 --> 00:01:31.070
And put the world on my plate!

00:01:31.070 --> 00:01:33.870
Wow wow wow! Eat the mountains!!

00:01:33.870 --> 00:01:36.440
Wow wow wow! Toriko!!

00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:39.040
Wow wow wow! Eat the oceans!!

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:43.310
Wow wow wow! Tori, Tori, Tori, Toriko!!

00:01:46.650 --> 00:01:48.820
Someone once said:

00:01:49.880 --> 00:01:52.690
There is a consommé-flavored waterfall,

00:01:52.690 --> 00:01:57.960
where white noodles as fine 
as silk thread gently flow...

00:01:57.960 --> 00:02:01.930
The Conoodle Falls!

00:02:03.700 --> 00:02:09.800
There is sand that looks like sugar 
candy when whittled away by waves,

00:02:09.800 --> 00:02:14.740
whose sweetness grows more 
with the salty tides...

00:02:15.080 --> 00:02:20.180
Under the sun, these little islands 
glitter the colors of the rainbow...

00:02:20.180 --> 00:02:23.920
The Rock Candy Isles!

00:02:24.350 --> 00:02:27.020
The world is in the Gourmet Age!

00:02:27.350 --> 00:02:32.560
An age in which people quest for 
yet unknown culinary delights!

00:02:34.790 --> 00:02:38.470
Toriko and Komatsu visited the 
Bellyfull City, Gourmet Town.

00:02:38.470 --> 00:02:41.940
Their purpose was to meet 
up with a certain person.

00:02:42.700 --> 00:02:47.570
Meanwhile, in order to obtain GOD, the 
ingredient that stands atop all others,

00:02:47.570 --> 00:02:50.610
the Gourmet Corp. first 
set their sights on a soup

00:02:50.610 --> 00:02:54.310
melted from the ice continent, which 
will make their Gourmet Cells evolve.

00:02:55.280 --> 00:02:57.950
The person Toriko had 
plans to meet up with was

00:02:57.950 --> 00:03:02.390
Gourmet Living National Treasure 
and legendary chef, Setsuno!

00:03:02.920 --> 00:03:05.290
And on her special menu is...

00:03:06.330 --> 00:03:09.260
Century Soup...

00:03:10.900 --> 00:03:15.730
Dreamtime! Setsuno's Century Soup!

00:03:19.140 --> 00:03:22.770
It'll be a little while 
before the soup is ready,

00:03:22.770 --> 00:03:27.350
so how about I make Garlic Bird and Egg Bowl?

00:03:27.350 --> 00:03:29.880
Really?! By all means, Granny Setsu!

00:03:46.300 --> 00:03:48.070
A-Amazing!

00:03:48.070 --> 00:03:50.830
She's doing all of the steps by herself...

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:53.100
And thoroughly, too!

00:03:54.640 --> 00:03:56.440
Setsuno's Diner is open!

00:03:56.440 --> 00:03:59.140
My eyes aren't playing tricks on 
me, are they, Section Chief Seki?!

00:04:01.950 --> 00:04:05.180
Here, drink some water and 
let's wait patiently, Komatsu.

00:04:05.450 --> 00:04:07.280
Thank you.

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:13.990
It's delicious! What kind of water is this?!

00:04:13.990 --> 00:04:16.760
It's easy to drink, like as light as air!

00:04:16.760 --> 00:04:20.360
It's Air Aqua, water that 
wells up from Aqua Mountain.

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:23.900
Wow! And that high class water is used 
as regular drinking water here...

00:04:23.900 --> 00:04:25.740
But that's Setsuno's Diner for you!

00:04:25.740 --> 00:04:30.040
And everything on the 
menu is first-rate food!

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:32.810
Yeah. Here's Granny Setsu's full course:

00:04:32.810 --> 00:04:37.150
For the hors d'oeuvre, Hundred Leaf 
Clover with Crunchy Fried Sesame...

00:04:34.380 --> 00:04:37.480
Hundred Leaf Clover with Crunchy Fried Sesame

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:41.280
For the soup, Consommé Magma Stew...

00:04:39.380 --> 00:04:41.880
Consommé Magma Stew

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:46.320
For the fish dish, Seared 
Royal Land Shark Sushi...

00:04:43.790 --> 00:04:46.620
Seared Royal Land Shark Sushi

00:04:46.820 --> 00:04:50.830
For the meat dish, Roast Ashurasaurus...

00:04:48.520 --> 00:04:51.030
Roast Ashurasaurus

00:04:51.030 --> 00:04:55.130
The main dish, ET Rice Balls...

00:04:52.930 --> 00:04:55.360
ET Rice Balls

00:04:55.560 --> 00:04:59.700
The salad, Grana Lettuce Caesar Salad...

00:04:57.270 --> 00:05:00.100
Grana Lettuce Caesar Salad

00:05:00.100 --> 00:05:04.540
For dessert, Oasis Melon Sherbet...

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:04.810
Oasis Melon Sherbet

00:05:04.810 --> 00:05:08.910
And the drink, Doham Spring Sake...

00:05:06.710 --> 00:05:09.240
Doham Spring Sake

00:05:09.810 --> 00:05:15.250
They've all been prepared 
by Knocking Master Jiro.

00:05:16.120 --> 00:05:18.690
Then they're all world-class dishes, huh?

00:05:18.690 --> 00:05:24.530
It's difficult to procure the 
ingredients for my full course.

00:05:24.530 --> 00:05:26.760
You can't usually get them in any store.

00:05:26.760 --> 00:05:29.430
So I had to ask Jiro-chan to track them down.

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:33.800
I break a camera, the scoops get away...

00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:36.540
Lately, I haven't had even 
a gram of good luck...

00:05:41.710 --> 00:05:44.240
The Chief is browsing the 
Internet for personal use!

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:47.350
And after he made <i>me</i> write a written 
explanation about the camera!

00:05:48.280 --> 00:05:50.820
Setsuno's Diner is open?!

00:05:50.820 --> 00:05:52.050
That's a scoop!

00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:55.990
Chief! Heaping good job!

00:05:55.990 --> 00:05:57.460
Oh, really?

00:05:57.460 --> 00:05:59.090
Wait, where have I seen that camera before...

00:05:59.090 --> 00:06:01.290
Hey, that's mine! Get back here!

00:06:06.270 --> 00:06:08.470
Paradise Rice!

00:06:10.140 --> 00:06:11.800
Seasoning, too!

00:06:11.800 --> 00:06:13.940
And the highest grade!

00:06:20.510 --> 00:06:23.380
10 yolks in there... A 10-yolked egg!

00:06:23.380 --> 00:06:25.680
Toriko-san, isn't that incredible?!

00:06:30.890 --> 00:06:32.120
All righty...

00:06:33.490 --> 00:06:35.790
It's ready. Here you are.

00:06:35.790 --> 00:06:39.930
Garlic Bird and Egg Bowl!

00:06:40.230 --> 00:06:42.430
Thank you for the food!

00:06:49.840 --> 00:06:53.580
The garlic flavor of the bird and 
the sweetness of the 10-yolked Egg

00:06:53.580 --> 00:06:55.610
blend in with the Paradise Rice!

00:06:55.610 --> 00:06:58.450
It's so delicious, I can't describe it!

00:06:58.450 --> 00:07:00.350
Granny Setsu, another bowl!

00:07:00.350 --> 00:07:01.250
You wolfed that down!

00:07:01.250 --> 00:07:04.020
Eat more slowly so you can 
appreciate the flavor!

00:07:04.020 --> 00:07:09.890
In any case, I detect the slight scent 
of sesame in this Bird and Egg Bowl...

00:07:12.100 --> 00:07:15.000
I'm impressed you noticed.

00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:20.970
I added a pinch of crushed sesame 
chestnut seeds to my broth.

00:07:20.970 --> 00:07:23.470
I'm learning a lot here!

00:07:23.470 --> 00:07:26.140
I bet Seven-Spice Blend 
would go well with it, too!

00:07:26.140 --> 00:07:28.780
That's an interesting idea.

00:07:28.780 --> 00:07:34.620
You've got a good sense of taste, power 
of observation, curiosity, imagination,

00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:37.720
and eroticism to boot...

00:07:37.720 --> 00:07:38.690
Oh, I wouldn't say...

00:07:38.690 --> 00:07:40.520
Eroticism?!

00:07:40.520 --> 00:07:44.090
I think she means you have the 
talent to make erotic dishes!

00:07:44.090 --> 00:07:46.160
What kind of dishes would that be?!

00:07:46.160 --> 00:07:49.130
I see, Komatsu-kun...

00:07:49.130 --> 00:07:51.630
You're someone I'll look forward to seeing...

00:07:52.230 --> 00:07:54.100
Well, it's ready.

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:57.370
My special menu...

00:07:57.370 --> 00:08:01.210
Century Soup!

00:08:05.710 --> 00:08:07.250
That's...

00:08:09.020 --> 00:08:11.050
...the legendary sou...

00:08:12.050 --> 00:08:13.390
Huh?

00:08:14.420 --> 00:08:17.830
Um, it's empty Setsuno-san...

00:08:19.090 --> 00:08:22.500
Is it so transparent that 
you can't even see it?

00:08:22.500 --> 00:08:24.730
You can smell it, can't you?

00:08:29.900 --> 00:08:33.840
An infinite number of ingredients 
are hitting my brain all at once!

00:08:33.840 --> 00:08:36.810
Are there that many ingredients 
condensed in the broth?!

00:08:39.080 --> 00:08:41.450
Section Chief Seki!

00:08:42.150 --> 00:08:44.990
What are all these people doing here?!

00:08:44.990 --> 00:08:49.060
It's because the Chief 
mentioned it on your blog!

00:08:49.960 --> 00:08:52.130
Excuse me! Move!

00:08:54.360 --> 00:08:57.060
That scent is chock-full of goodness!

00:08:58.370 --> 00:09:01.000
Noisy out there...

00:09:01.000 --> 00:09:04.700
But with the aroma of this legendary 
soup, I suppose that's natural.

00:09:05.770 --> 00:09:08.840
Many ingredients, representatives 
of this century,

00:09:08.840 --> 00:09:11.480
have been stewing for half a year.

00:09:11.480 --> 00:09:16.620
I remove the scum and all that's left 
is the deliciousness of the broth.

00:09:16.620 --> 00:09:22.660
That is this Century Soup!

00:09:22.660 --> 00:09:25.560
Here you are. Drink up!

00:09:25.560 --> 00:09:27.560
Finally!

00:09:29.830 --> 00:09:31.960
Thank you for the food!

00:09:38.340 --> 00:09:41.540
I can't get enough!

00:09:43.280 --> 00:09:45.880
Crystal clear soup!

00:09:52.920 --> 00:09:57.160
Even though it's as colorless as 
water, it has such a rich flavor!

00:09:57.160 --> 00:09:59.320
Wonderful...

00:09:59.320 --> 00:10:00.490
Well?

00:10:00.490 --> 00:10:03.090
How's the Century Soup?

00:10:03.630 --> 00:10:05.860
Even though the taste of the 
ingredients you used in the broth

00:10:05.860 --> 00:10:07.130
are packed in there, 
they're not overpowering,

00:10:07.130 --> 00:10:08.930
and it feels refreshing going down!

00:10:08.930 --> 00:10:11.140
I've never had that with soup before!

00:10:11.140 --> 00:10:12.900
Right, Komatsu?

00:10:16.540 --> 00:10:18.010
Komatsu, what's wrong?

00:10:19.010 --> 00:10:20.640
Komatsu!

00:10:21.580 --> 00:10:23.380
Sorry!

00:10:23.380 --> 00:10:27.420
Once in a while, I get so moved, 
I become immersed in the flavor!

00:10:27.420 --> 00:10:28.790
How was the soup?

00:10:28.790 --> 00:10:32.460
Boy! It was absolutely delicious!

00:10:32.460 --> 00:10:34.720
Thank you, Setsuno-san!

00:10:34.720 --> 00:10:37.360
Your soup is just magnificent!

00:10:38.830 --> 00:10:40.660
I'm glad you like it.

00:10:40.660 --> 00:10:45.500
I'm not sure if Silk Chicken Bones is 
one of the ingredients of the broth...

00:10:45.500 --> 00:10:46.670
but am I right?

00:10:46.670 --> 00:10:52.310
My, my! After just a few sips, you 
can pick out one of the ingredients?!

00:10:52.310 --> 00:10:55.210
And you've got some Mineral 
Coconut in there too, right?

00:10:55.210 --> 00:10:59.550
That's it! I thought I 
detected a familiar flavor!

00:10:59.550 --> 00:11:00.920
Impressive as always, Toriko-san!

00:11:00.920 --> 00:11:02.350
These guys...

00:11:02.350 --> 00:11:04.050
The only thing...

00:11:04.350 --> 00:11:07.290
I feel like there's something missing...

00:11:07.820 --> 00:11:09.660
An ingredient?

00:11:10.730 --> 00:11:13.100
Toriko! Komatsu-kun!

00:11:13.760 --> 00:11:15.260
Follow me!

00:11:15.260 --> 00:11:19.570
I'll give you a tour of my kitchen, 
where I do all my preparation.

00:11:20.570 --> 00:11:23.540
Granny Setsu, your... kitchen?!

00:11:23.540 --> 00:11:26.510
Your kitchen is in another place?!

00:11:26.510 --> 00:11:28.580
My heart's going pitter-pat!

00:11:28.580 --> 00:11:30.410
Before that, Granny Setsu...!

00:11:30.880 --> 00:11:33.110
Can I drink all the soup?

00:11:33.110 --> 00:11:35.620
And can I eat the other food that's left?

00:11:35.620 --> 00:11:37.090
Just get over here!

00:11:40.390 --> 00:11:42.490
It's down here.

00:11:42.490 --> 00:11:44.990
There's a kitchen in the basement?!

00:11:44.990 --> 00:11:47.090
I didn't know it 'til now either!

00:11:47.090 --> 00:11:52.300
The upstairs kitchen is for 
putting on the finishing touches.

00:11:52.300 --> 00:11:59.670
But really, the bulk of my diner, Setsuko's 
Diner, is here in my prep space.

00:12:17.090 --> 00:12:18.660
Oh my gosh!

00:12:18.660 --> 00:12:21.390
This is Setsuko's Diner's kitchen!

00:12:21.390 --> 00:12:24.200
Who knew there was a place like 
this right under our feet?!

00:12:24.200 --> 00:12:27.430
Do you do all of the preparation down here?

00:12:28.940 --> 00:12:31.840
I think you already know this, 
Komatsu-kun, but it's safe to say that

00:12:31.840 --> 00:12:36.480
how a dish turns out is mostly 
decided in the preparation stage.

00:12:36.480 --> 00:12:37.780
Yes...

00:12:37.780 --> 00:12:41.380
Being that it's underground, the 
customers never see the kitchen,

00:12:41.380 --> 00:12:45.780
but it's the backbone of this restaurant.

00:12:47.250 --> 00:12:51.660
Strictly speaking, no one is allowed 
down here aside from the staff.

00:12:51.660 --> 00:12:53.490
Thank you!

00:12:53.490 --> 00:12:55.430
Setsuno-san, this precious place is...

00:12:57.200 --> 00:12:58.100
Huh?

00:12:59.160 --> 00:13:01.070
Disgraceful...

00:13:01.070 --> 00:13:04.000
Any restaurant worth its 
salt has live ingredients.

00:13:04.000 --> 00:13:06.770
But ferocious animals?!

00:13:07.910 --> 00:13:09.640
Spa Monkeys...

00:13:09.640 --> 00:13:12.340
You soak them with citron in hot 
water, and when the temperature

00:13:11.080 --> 00:13:17.010
Spa Monkey  (Mammalian 
Beast) Capture Level 37

00:13:12.340 --> 00:13:14.180
reaches precisely 42 degrees,

00:13:14.180 --> 00:13:17.220
a wonderful, refreshing yet 
delicate broth results.

00:13:18.150 --> 00:13:21.190
The warming machine is on the fritz!

00:13:22.350 --> 00:13:25.920
Recently, this wheel's been sticking.

00:13:25.920 --> 00:13:26.990
Glance!

00:13:28.390 --> 00:13:30.760
Out of the way, Komatsu!

00:13:30.760 --> 00:13:32.960
2-Fold Spiked Punch!

00:13:37.470 --> 00:13:41.510
Uh... Normally, do you 
turn that, Setsuko-san?

00:13:41.510 --> 00:13:43.270
What <i>are</i> you?!

00:13:43.540 --> 00:13:46.640
Don't tell me, that's also where 
you prepare the Century Soup...?!

00:13:46.640 --> 00:13:48.040
You're way off-base.

00:13:48.040 --> 00:13:49.510
Wrong again!

00:13:51.310 --> 00:13:55.350
If you look closely, there are incredible 
ingredients all over the place...

00:13:55.350 --> 00:13:56.820
Peach Potatoes!

00:13:56.820 --> 00:13:58.520
They're supposed to be really hard to handle.

00:13:58.520 --> 00:14:01.890
It's said the skin is so slippery, 
you could peel 1000 potatoes

00:14:01.890 --> 00:14:03.960
in the time it takes you 
to peel one Peach Potato!

00:14:03.960 --> 00:14:07.530
That's Stiff Leek! It has 
such an adhesive force

00:14:07.530 --> 00:14:10.670
that it takes hundreds of 
cuts to get it to come apart!

00:14:11.430 --> 00:14:12.970
I see...

00:14:12.970 --> 00:14:16.670
The reason Setsuno-san only opens 
the restaurant once a month

00:14:16.670 --> 00:14:20.040
is that it takes so much 
time to prepare everything!

00:14:20.040 --> 00:14:22.540
You're wrong, Komatsu-kun!

00:14:29.650 --> 00:14:31.920
Come on, over here! Quick!

00:14:31.920 --> 00:14:34.590
Is there a point to crossing over like that?!

00:14:36.260 --> 00:14:37.430
Like that.

00:14:47.170 --> 00:14:48.570
Um...

00:14:49.470 --> 00:14:54.210
Setsuno-san, why do you open the 
restaurant only once a month?

00:14:54.210 --> 00:14:56.410
I told you, it's whenever I feel like it!

00:14:56.410 --> 00:15:00.280
Or more precisely, it's not 
when <i>I</i> feel like it...  {saving the line here}

00:15:01.220 --> 00:15:03.620
It's when the ingredients feel like it!

00:15:03.920 --> 00:15:05.990
When the ingredients feel like it?

00:15:05.990 --> 00:15:07.790
Komatsu-kun...

00:15:07.790 --> 00:15:10.020
You think that a chef chooses her ingredients

00:15:10.020 --> 00:15:12.690
and then makes the food, don't you?

00:15:14.830 --> 00:15:17.030
How presumptuous.

00:15:17.030 --> 00:15:20.570
As long as you think that, 
you'll only be half a chef.

00:15:21.200 --> 00:15:22.640
It's the opposite.

00:15:22.640 --> 00:15:27.110
The ingredients choose the 
customers and the chef.

00:15:27.670 --> 00:15:29.680
The ingredients choose...?!

00:15:29.680 --> 00:15:35.650
I just ask the ingredients 
how they feel every day.

00:15:35.650 --> 00:15:41.350
Whether the restaurant is open or closed 
depends entirely on the ingredients.

00:15:41.890 --> 00:15:43.660
B-But that's...

00:15:43.660 --> 00:15:46.390
Even though your kitchen 
is set up so perfectly...

00:15:47.490 --> 00:15:50.830
One of these days, you'll 
understand, Komatsu-kun...

00:15:50.830 --> 00:15:53.000
One of these days, I'm sure...

00:15:54.230 --> 00:15:55.970
Well, here we are.

00:15:55.970 --> 00:16:00.240
<i>This</i> is where I prepare the Century Soup!

00:16:05.240 --> 00:16:08.910
I-It's huge!

00:16:08.910 --> 00:16:12.020
This must be the legendary 
soup simmering pot!

00:16:12.020 --> 00:16:16.320
I've never seen a pot this big before!

00:16:25.760 --> 00:16:27.100
Setsuno-san!

00:16:27.100 --> 00:16:29.570
Really, what are you?!

00:16:29.570 --> 00:16:32.240
Come on, Komatsu! We're climbing up, too!

00:16:32.240 --> 00:16:34.410
W-Wait for me!

00:16:58.200 --> 00:17:00.860
Wow!!

00:17:01.330 --> 00:17:02.730
I'm moved!

00:17:02.730 --> 00:17:07.000
Is this the Century Soup, with 
all the ingredients soaking in?!

00:17:07.000 --> 00:17:08.670
I'm shocked...

00:17:08.670 --> 00:17:12.010
Even before serving, the soup 
is already so transparent...

00:17:12.980 --> 00:17:17.680
That's because I've been skimming 
off the scum for half a year.  {wish there were a nicer term for it than "scum"}

00:17:17.680 --> 00:17:22.750
But actually, this soup... is incomplete.

00:17:22.750 --> 00:17:28.060
There really are Silk Chicken Bones 
and Mineral Coconuts in here.

00:17:28.060 --> 00:17:29.690
And Motor Onions, too!

00:17:29.690 --> 00:17:31.190
What a spectacular lineup!

00:17:31.190 --> 00:17:32.760
Granny Setsu, you're amazing!

00:17:32.760 --> 00:17:34.400
I know.

00:17:34.400 --> 00:17:39.770
But I still say this soup is incomplete!

00:17:40.600 --> 00:17:43.870
If you look carefully, you can 
see a German Swordfish bone!

00:17:43.870 --> 00:17:47.110
It's said it won't dissolve and you 
can't get the stink out for months!

00:17:47.110 --> 00:17:49.010
But I don't smell it one bit!

00:17:49.010 --> 00:17:50.410
It's uncanny, Granny Setsu!

00:17:50.410 --> 00:17:52.210
Yes, yes, I'm uncanny!

00:17:52.210 --> 00:17:53.720
However!

00:17:53.720 --> 00:17:58.690
This Century Soup is still incomplete!

00:18:00.760 --> 00:18:03.830
You finally hear me?! Pay more attention!

00:18:04.890 --> 00:18:06.590
What do you mean?

00:18:06.590 --> 00:18:13.270
Originally, Century Soup existed in nature.

00:18:13.870 --> 00:18:15.540
Really?!

00:18:15.540 --> 00:18:17.240
That's the first I've heard!

00:18:18.110 --> 00:18:21.940
A long time ago, Jiro-chan 
scooped some up for me.

00:18:22.840 --> 00:18:27.010
Just one taste and I couldn't forget it...

00:18:27.010 --> 00:18:31.120
This soup is my imitation of that.

00:18:31.120 --> 00:18:34.550
Th-This is plenty good...

00:18:34.550 --> 00:18:36.820
But it's incomplete?

00:18:36.820 --> 00:18:41.160
In my heart, I know it's 
not a perfect recreation. {because Jiro didn't bring it to her, and she'll eventually realize that...}

00:18:41.160 --> 00:18:44.060
But... it's delicious, right, Toriko-san?

00:18:44.060 --> 00:18:45.630
Too delicious!

00:18:45.630 --> 00:18:47.530
You're having too much, Toriko!

00:18:47.530 --> 00:18:54.970
Could the Century Soup that's found in 
nature be even more delicious than this?

00:18:54.970 --> 00:18:56.340
Who knows?

00:18:56.340 --> 00:18:58.910
It's hard to describe the flavor...

00:18:58.910 --> 00:18:59.710
Komatsu-kun!

00:18:59.710 --> 00:19:00.350
Yes?!

00:19:00.350 --> 00:19:05.380
When you drank this soup, you 
said it was "missing something".

00:19:05.380 --> 00:19:06.550
Yes...

00:19:06.550 --> 00:19:09.660
Right... You were exactly right.

00:19:09.660 --> 00:19:14.390
I believe the real thing had 
one more flavor added...

00:19:14.390 --> 00:19:18.630
But I have no idea what that one thing was...

00:19:18.630 --> 00:19:22.800
Oh, I didn't mean... It 
was just my impression!

00:19:22.800 --> 00:19:25.500
After all, I've never tried the original...

00:19:25.500 --> 00:19:30.140
Why do you think I brought you 
two down here to my kitchen?

00:19:31.310 --> 00:19:36.080
Presidents of nations, 
wealthy people, gourmands...

00:19:36.080 --> 00:19:41.120
When it comes to my cooking, I don't 
give a fig about any of their opinions!

00:19:42.050 --> 00:19:46.420
But you two, I've fallen in love 
with your tastes and sensibilities.

00:19:46.860 --> 00:19:54.430
I thought that just maybe you 
two could complete this soup.

00:19:55.400 --> 00:19:59.870
I brought you here so you could see 
exactly what I put in the soup.

00:19:59.870 --> 00:20:03.570
But... I wouldn't know how to complete it...

00:20:05.710 --> 00:20:08.380
You don't want to try it...?

00:20:08.380 --> 00:20:10.810
The real Century Soup?

00:20:10.810 --> 00:20:12.450
I do! I do!

00:20:13.080 --> 00:20:15.450
I knew you would, Toriko!

00:20:15.450 --> 00:20:19.420
Right, Komatsu? You wanna try 
drinking the real soup, don't you?!

00:20:19.420 --> 00:20:22.690
Y-Yes! I want to give it a try!

00:20:22.690 --> 00:20:23.930
The time is right!

00:20:23.930 --> 00:20:27.730
Century Soup only appears 
once every 100 years!

00:20:27.730 --> 00:20:30.900
Which is why it's called "Century Soup"!

00:20:30.900 --> 00:20:35.240
Right now, there's a man in 
town who knows a lot about it.

00:20:35.240 --> 00:20:40.310
He's gathered Gourmet Hunters from around 
the world to try and get that soup!

00:20:41.410 --> 00:20:45.680
I'm sure he would hire the two 
of you in a flash, Toriko.

00:20:45.680 --> 00:20:47.980
Take Komatsu-kun with you!

00:20:47.980 --> 00:20:49.950
Drink the genuine Century Soup

00:20:49.950 --> 00:20:54.590
and then make a brilliant 
Century Soup of your own!

00:20:59.900 --> 00:21:02.930
The best place to go for 
information in this town is...

00:21:13.440 --> 00:21:19.110
Is the night wind, caressing my cheek

00:21:19.650 --> 00:21:25.390
proof the world is spinning, I wonder?

00:21:26.120 --> 00:21:32.630
Each time I move out, the 
direction of the wind changes.

00:21:33.030 --> 00:21:37.570
Maybe that’s telling me something.

00:21:38.830 --> 00:21:42.670
I was searching for what happiness meant.

00:21:42.670 --> 00:21:46.040
Aiming for the island in my dreams,

00:21:46.040 --> 00:21:50.510
on a journey with no end!

00:21:52.350 --> 00:21:55.480
Blown by the winds of tomorrow,

00:21:55.480 --> 00:21:58.620
drifting off to who-knows-where,

00:21:58.620 --> 00:22:04.620
amid the waves of time.

00:22:07.460 --> 00:22:09.560
Gourmet News!

00:22:10.360 --> 00:22:12.130
I'm your host, Tina!

00:22:12.130 --> 00:22:16.270
Don't you feel like having a heaping 
helping of Garlic Chicken and Egg Bowl?!

00:22:16.270 --> 00:22:19.910
Or at least a bowl of 
rice with an egg on top!

00:22:20.770 --> 00:22:22.140
We're out of eggs!

00:22:22.480 --> 00:22:23.940
But that's fine!

00:22:23.940 --> 00:22:28.450
I'll introduce eggs over 
rice without the eggs!

00:22:30.820 --> 00:22:34.450
Pour milk and soy sauce on rice?

00:22:34.450 --> 00:22:35.790
Seriously?!

00:22:37.790 --> 00:22:40.160
Well... Thank you for the food...

00:22:44.530 --> 00:22:47.800
It's delicious! But why?!

00:22:47.800 --> 00:22:50.970
It tastes just like a heaping 
helping of eggs over rice!

00:22:53.810 --> 00:22:54.910
More!

00:22:54.910 --> 00:22:56.570
There isn't any more?!

00:22:56.570 --> 00:23:00.010
Now I miss the taste of eggs even more!

00:23:00.010 --> 00:23:02.310
Granny Setsu!

00:23:02.310 --> 00:23:04.480
Now, on to the next story!

00:23:06.850 --> 00:23:09.280
The place where those who chase their dreams gather.

00:23:09.280 --> 00:23:10.590
These men have risen up...

00:23:10.590 --> 00:23:13.080
in pursuit of a once-in-a-century flavor!

00:23:13.770 --> 00:23:17.330
Meeting at the Saloon! Rivalry Between Gourmet Hunters!

00:23:17.550 --> 00:23:19.490
Look forward to another heaping helping of fun!
